 By Neil Irwin and Courtenay Brown &middot; Nov 13, 2026 
 
 
 Today, we look at the weak links of the global trade system — which helps explain this era of rolling supply disruptions and crises in which we seem to be living.

 Plus, the latest inflation data suggests falling fuel prices are not translating into relief across America's supply chain. 😖 Situational awareness: Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent, appearing on CNBC this morning , pointed to the Commerce Department as the holdout in restricting Singaporean company Megaspeed from obtaining advanced chips.

 It amounted to the behind-the-scenes tensions with Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick, first reported by our colleagues Maria Curi and Marc Caputo, spilling out into the open. More here . Today's newsletter, edited by Jeffrey Cane and copy edited by Katie Lewis, is 865 words, a 3.5-minute read. 

 
 
